# MASTER PROMPT: Build a Complete Offline Quick Billing & Mini POS Desktop Application

## 1. Your Role

Act as a senior software architect, senior React developer, senior ASP.NET Core developer, database designer, UI/UX designer, QA engineer, and Windows desktop deployment specialist.

Build a complete, production-oriented, offline-first Quick Billing and Mini POS application for a small retail shop.

Do not create only a prototype, static dashboard, or UI mockup. Build a functional application with working frontend components, backend APIs, database persistence, stock management, billing, reporting, Excel export, and Windows deployment support.

The code must be clean, modular, reusable, readable, maintainable, and beginner-friendly.

Explain important implementation decisions and provide exact terminal commands and file paths.

---

## 2. Primary Goal

Create a Windows 10/11 64-bit desktop-oriented billing application that:

- Works without an internet connection after installation.
- Can be distributed to another compatible Windows computer through a Windows Setup `.exe` installer.
- Uses a separate local database on each computer.
- Does not require a cloud server, external API, or internet connection for normal operation.
- Stores all products, sales, stock, and payment information locally.
- Supports Excel export and local database backup and restore.
- Provides a modern, fast, professional retail POS interface.
- Allows the owner to customize product cards and other UI components easily without modifying unrelated business logic.

The application is designed primarily for one computer and one local database at a time. Cross-device synchronization is not required.

