### Permanent price change vs bill-specific price

These are different operations.

Permanent price changes update the product's current selling price.

A bill-specific price override affects only the current sale item and must not silently change the product's permanent price.

Every sale item must store a snapshot of the actual unit price used for that sale.

Historical invoices and reports must continue to display the original sold price even if the product price changes later.

Price overrides must be validated by the backend. Do not trust client-submitted totals or prices.

